Z||000002||BAM-BAM||04-28-2000||08:01 AM||||  Hey, have a go with the cobra head joystick type of shifter handle. I got mine from the dealer for around $10.00 for the vynal; the leather is $40.00. I'll go with the leather once I have the interior redone. But, it's awesome and gives the interior a modern look and feel. It fits purfect. just remove the locking clip(keep it) and pull the old one off, slip the new one on, replace the clip(you kept that...right?)and your good to go. Oh, you may have to readjust the boot a little, that takes seconds.<P> Late, BAM OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>P.S. The new shift handle is out of a 95 Grand Prix.<p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 04-28-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000003||Monkeyman||04-28-2000||10:19 AM||||I bought an almost brand new looking leather shift knob at the local boneyard last fall for $10.  It was out of a current generation Camaro, but it's the same in the previous generation.  Happy Hunting!||||reg||1
