Z||000009||theogre||04-29-2000||02:50 PM||||how short you could cut down the lever depends allot on what knob you are going to put on. It's not as much a problem of getting to the grears as it is of room for the boot to bunch up in. If the boot is pushed down to far you end up with it binding in the hardware undernieth and likly breaking the indicator slide.<P>It's not easy to cut down. You need to take it apart and remove the core. then you cut the shaft and mill a new slot for the knob and new slots for the clip. then you cut the core by the same amount you cut the shaft. finally you file all the egdes clean and put the whole thing back together.<P>kind of allot of work, and you're likely only going to get maybe a inch shorter using GM knobs. GM knobs seem to all use about the same amount of shaft for mounting.||||reg||1
Z||000010||DaRkLoRD||04-29-2000||05:40 PM||||What if a custom boot were used, or even an aftermarket manual shifter boot?<P>There's probably a reason why that won't work..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Monkeyman||04-29-2000||06:45 PM||||A manual shift boot would probably be too wide to work.  I know it would be alot of trouble, but I think an inch would be just about right.  Looks like they took something out of an Escort the way it is now.||||reg||1
